&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The community you will join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Airbnb&#39;s mission is to create a world where people can Belong Anywhere. We&#39;re seeking a NextStay Fellow to help pursue that mission as a hands-on Technical Program Manager (TPM) in our engineering organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;The NextStay Fellowship is a launchpad: you&#39;ll join with a strong program management foundation and grow into the full scope and ambiguity of the role, supported by experienced TPMs and engineering partners invested in your success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A typical day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;Lead execution of a project with a defined scope and approach, turning direction from your manager or senior TPMs into a concrete, realistic plan built around known constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;Break work into trackable pieces and use input and output metrics to monitor progress, surfacing slippage before it becomes a problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;Lead alignment of the project team and hold contributors accountable to deliverables and milestones, while anticipating the next set of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;Consult team members or leaders to identify risks and mitigation options; track and manage risks you&#39;ve already identified through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;Communicate the project&#39;s vision and success criteria clearly to your project team and stakeholders, and re-evaluate strategy with guidance from leadership on when to pivot versus stay the course.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;Ask the right questions to surface potential technical gaps, working collaboratively with engineers and applying a working understanding of sound technical principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;Actively participate in cultural and functional excellence activities—such as Connect apprenticeship (curriculum contribution, mentorship), diversity and inclusion programming (Airfinity, Blocking Bias training), or hackathons—and demonstrate Airbnb&#39;s core values in everyday interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The difference you will make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;As a NextStay Fellow you&#39;ll own execution of technical programs spanning multiple engineering, product, and operations teams over several quarters — turning objectives set with your manager and senior TPMs into milestones, delivery plans, and team alignment. Working under the guidance of senior TPMs, you&#39;ll hold the program accountable to deliverables while managing scope, schedule, and quality trade-offs, re-planning proactively as conditions change and escalating the decisions that carry real business risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Core manager competencies include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scope Management&lt;/strong&gt; – Partners with the team to define boundaries and milestones against program objectives, enabling informed trade-off conversations and preventing scope creep across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Schedule Management&lt;/strong&gt; – Breaks work into sized, sequenced pieces with clear dependencies, builds a schedule with technical partners, and communicates changes as they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality&lt;/strong&gt; – Establishes the expected level of quality during planning and treats it as a fixed constraint alongside schedule and scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication&lt;/strong&gt; – Keeps stakeholders informed early and often, especially when unexpected issues occur.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt; – Identifies stakeholders, listens to their concerns, and sets expectations appropriately throughout the project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk Identification&lt;/strong&gt; – Surfaces upstream and downstream dependencies and risks early, analyzing them within the context of the overall plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk Mitigation&lt;/strong&gt; – Aligns the team on the mitigations that matter most and executes the recommended path with senior TPMs, so the team can respond calmly if a risk materializes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Eligibility Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;We are honored to support transitioning service members. To be considered for this fellowship, please ensure you meet the following criteria:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;You are an active-duty service member currently enrolled in the USSOCOM Warrior Care Program, Career Transition Internship, or a similar program. &lt;em&gt;(Please note: DoD SkillBridge participants are not eligible at this time).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;You are able to begin your Career Transition Fellowship by November 2026 and complete at least 120 days of the program before your military transition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;You are within 180 days of your military transition (separation, ETS, or retirement) at the time of your fellowship starts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;You can provide written approval from your chain of command authorizing your participation before final selection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Typically 2 years of relevant experience, with a BS or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science or a related technical field, or equivalent experience. Most TPMs spend roughly 2.5 to 4 years at this level, with a minimum of one year before progressing, before moving into a role with more ambiguity and scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Able to build a solid, realistic plan based on identified constraints and track progress using input and output metrics. Comfortable managing scope, schedule, and quality trade-offs, and open to on-the-job training and guidance on prioritization early on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Surfaces upstream and downstream dependencies and risks early, aligns the team on how to reduce the impact of the ones that matter most, and drives identified risks through to resolution — partnering with senior TPMs on the recommended path so the team can respond calmly if a risk materializes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Judgment:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable working collaboratively with engineers; asks the right questions to surface technical gaps and applies sound technical judgement to evaluate solutions and tradeoffs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Exchanges information clearly and seeks clarification when needed. Communicates project vision and success criteria effectively to the project team and stakeholders. Strong written and verbal communicator who can answer questions directly related to their project, and manages the project team to deliverables and milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Takes ownership of programs and drives them forward, exercising sound judgment on when to resolve independently versus when to escalate&amp;nbsp; and partnering with senior TPMs on the decisions that carry real risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our commitment to inclusion &amp;amp; belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the best and brightest people from the broadest talent pool possible. We believe a diversity of ideas fosters innovation and engagement, and allows us to attract the best people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. If you need assistance, or a reasonable accommodation during the application and recruiting process, please let your recruiter know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important information about full-time opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;We cannot guarantee that this project will turn into a full time position. Full-time employment is dependent on headcount availability and business hiring needs. However, we would love to introduce you to the world of Airbnb and other tech companies within our network, as you transition out of the NextStay Program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb values diversity &amp;amp; belonging and is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. All individuals seeking employment at Airbnb are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, gender, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, or any other legally protected characteristic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we’ll take care of you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career or degree level. This role may also be eligible for benefits and Employee Travel Credits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$151,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$151,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is redefining the world&#39;s approach to accommodation and travel. We are creating highly local, personal and authentic experiences for our host and guest community around the world. Our platform connects millions of people a year and furthers our mission to create a world where anyone can belong anywhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To power the global Airbnb community, we are building a world-class payments platform - one that currently supports 191 countries, 63 currencies, connects dozens of payment providers and banks, and processes billions of dollars per year for all of Airbnb’s business units. As the platform grows, we’ll be adding new payment partners, establishing licensed payments companies around the world, and building innovative payment experiences and financial products for our guests and hosts. Our goal? To create a future where transparent, simple, and familiar payment solutions can empower people, entrepreneurs and communities on our global marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is seeking an experienced and strategic Payment Partnerships Manager to drive the vision, execution, and ongoing performance of our partner network supporting how we pay out to our global host community across 200+ markets. Reporting to the Head of Payment Partnerships, this role is pivotal in managing the partnerships that ensure our hosts are paid reliably, efficiently, compliantly and in alignment with our growth and platform goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead business development, deal negotiation, and strategic relationship management for a portfolio of high-value payment partners. With a focus on impact and long-term alignment, you&#39;ll help craft our partner landscape, structure and renegotiate commercial agreements, and serve as a critical voice in expanding and optimizing how payments to hosts are enabled around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strategic Partner Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve our payout partner strategy in collaboration with the broader Payments, Product, Compliance and Finance teams to ensure coverage, performance, and alignment with Airbnb’s strategic and financial goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify the right partners in each market, structure new deals, and renegotiate existing relationships to optimize for cost, reliability, reach, and innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive global deal execution for payouts—developing commercial structures, navigating regional regulatory constraints, and shaping contracts to meet Airbnb’s evolving needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Relationship Management &amp;amp; Performance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and cultivate high-impact relationships with financial institutions, payment processors, banks, and other key partners, managing executive-level engagement to ensure Airbnb is a priority client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor partner performance rigorously, identify gaps or opportunities, and lead cross-functional efforts to address issues or evolve terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic business reviews and act as the point of escalation and problem resolution for performance or operational misalignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Payments Strategy &amp;amp; Influence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the ongoing scaling of Airbnb’s payout infrastructure—ensuring that partner decisions reflect regional needs, market conditions, cost structures, and regulatory environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Legal, Treasury, Risk, Product, Engineering, and Global Operations to align execution with global strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of industry and macroeconomic changes affecting international payments and proactively bring forward opportunities and risk mitigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in the payments or fintech industry, with at least 8 years in strategic partnerships, business development, or enterprise account management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in owning commercial negotiations and managing multi-million dollar partnerships that balance customer experience, innovation, and financial return.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to craft and execute partner strategies that result in measurable business growth and process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of global payment methods, financial products, and cross-border payout solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of payments cost structure (e.g., interchange, chargebacks, FX, treasury flow), and experience optimizing it through partner levers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in resolving partner conflicts or escalations, ideally across multiple markets or regulatory contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International payments experience, especially in marketplace or platform models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in platform organizations advising internal stakeholders on partner enablement strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with regulators or regulated partners in cross-border payout environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or equivalent advanced degree is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;This position is US - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. While the position is Remote Eligible, you must live in a state where Airbnb Payments, Inc. (a subsidiary of Airbnb, Inc.) is a registered entity. Approved remote states include: Alabama, California, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Minnesota, Mississippi, Nevada, New Jersey, New York, North Carolina, Ohio, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Tennessee, Texas, and Washington. This list is continuously evolving, so please check back with us if the state you live in is excluded. If your position is employed by another Airbnb entity, your recruiter will inform you what states you are eligible to work from.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We strive to also provide a disability inclusive application and interview process. If you are a candidate with a disability and require reasonable accommodation in order to submit an application, please contact us at: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;mailto:reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;. Please include your full name, the role you’re applying for and the accommodation necessary to assist you with the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;We ask that you only reach out to us if you are a candidate whose disability prevents you from being able to complete our online application.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb values diversity &amp;amp; belonging and is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. All individuals seeking employment at Airbnb are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, gender, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, or any other legally protected characteristic.&lt;/p&gt;
