&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb&#39;s Creative Studio is part of the team that establishes and maintains the voice — and the judgment — behind everything we write, generate, and publish at scale. You&#39;ll sit alongside writers and creative directors in a group that thinks about language the way a great designer thinks about visuals: with precision, taste, and an instinct for what&#39;s right versus what&#39;s merely correct. Your closest cross-functional partner will be Marketing Technology, whose teams build and tune the language models and editorial tooling you&#39;ll help shape. You&#39;ll also partner regularly with Legal, Trust, and Localization to ensure editorial standards and processes hold up across markets, languages, and regulatory considerations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be responsible for shaping and maintaining Airbnb&#39;s brand voice and guidelines, training and refining the AI models that generate copy at scale, and serving as the final line of editorial judgment on AI-generated output before it reaches the world. This role is for someone whose taste and standards quietly define what &quot;sounds like the brand&quot; means, extended into an AI-assisted production pipeline. You won&#39;t just be proofreading — you&#39;ll be defining what &quot;good&quot; means for a system that writes at a scale no human team could match alone, and making sure it never loses the craft, warmth, and precision that language deserves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve Airbnb’s brand voice, tone, and editorial guidelines, ensuring they’re clear, opinionated, and usable by both humans and AI systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing Technology teams to train, fine-tune, and evaluate language models against brand voice standards, providing the editorial judgment that shapes what “on-brand” means at a model level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and refine AI-generated copy across campaigns, product, and marketing surfaces — catching not just errors, but tone, nuance, and craft issues an automated system would miss.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain scalable editorial QA processes for AI-generated content, defining what requires human review versus what can ship autonomously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate brand guidelines into structured inputs (style guides, prompt frameworks, training examples) that improve model output over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally to develop new internal tools that support editorial review, model training, and content QA, bringing an editorial point of view to how these tools are structured and used.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps in the current tooling ecosystem and help scope, prioritize, and define requirements for new tools that improve editorial efficiency and consistency at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pilot new tools with editorial and creative teams, gathering feedback and iterating on both functionality and language before wider rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a senior editorial voice in select creative reviews, giving direct, high-bar feedback to writers, creative directors, and AI workflows alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Trust, and Localization teams to ensure editorial standards and processes hold up across markets, languages, and regulatory considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and elevate writing and editorial talent across the org, setting the standard for what excellent, brand-true language looks like.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on how language models evolve, and continuously push the editorial standards and training methods that keep AI-generated copy at a craft level worth publishing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively seek out opportunities across the company for more efficient copy creation or delivery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify where language and voice consistency is breaking down at scale, and fix it at the system level — not just the sentence level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure content within the screens featured in our marketing materials are product-accurate, and efficiently created.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of editorial, copywriting, or brand voice experience, ideally at a Creative Director or Senior Editor level within an in-house brand team, agency, or publication known for editorial excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated, exacting eye for language — grammar and style are table stakes; what matters more is taste, rhythm, and judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or maintaining brand voice guidelines at scale across a global, multi-market brand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience working with or training AI/language models. You understand how models learn from examples and feedback, and you know how to give feedback that actually improves output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating as both a hands-on editor (line-editing real copy) and a systems thinker (defining standards that scale beyond your own review).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills, particularly with Engineering/Technology, Legal, and Localization teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort not just editing, but also writing; this role will craft brand guidelines, copy within tooling, and messaging within product screens.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The confidence to be the final word on language… and the humility to know when a guideline needs to evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio or body of work that reflects a distinctive, well-crafted brand voice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to simplify complex problems and create clarity in ambiguous, fast-moving environments.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Preferred skill-sets:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a company with a well-known editorial voice or brand language system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with prompt engineering, fine-tuning workflows, or structured content systems used to train generative models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience localizing or adapting brand voice across multiple languages and cultural contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in both traditional editorial craft (journalism, publishing, advertising copywriting) and modern content operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
